Subject: [PATCH] EvView: do not skip layout while the current page is loading

ev_view_size_allocate returned early while priv->loading was set. The
flag is set while drawing a page whose texture is not ready yet, and
cleared only when that page is drawn again. During a fast zoom-out the
scroll position can end up outside the shrunken document, the page is
never drawn, and the skipped allocation is not requested again: the
adjustment keeps its old, too large upper bound and the view shows
empty space. Evince 46.3 only skips layout when there is no document.

---
--- a/libview/ev-view.c
+++ b/libview/ev-view.c
@@ -4392,7 +4392,7 @@
 	EvView *view = EV_VIEW (widget);
 	EvViewPrivate *priv = GET_PRIVATE (view);
 
-	if (!priv->document || ev_view_is_loading (view))
+	if (!priv->document)
 		return;
 
 	if (priv->sizing_mode == EV_SIZING_FIT_WIDTH ||
